---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Roy Li | Entrepreneur and Public Voice">
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Vancouver-Langara · British Columbia</div>
          <h1>Less Bureaucracy.<br />More B.C.</h1>
          <p class="lead">Roy Li is a tech entrepreneur and public voice focused on safer communities, balanced budgets, cutting red tape, and rebuilding confidence for families, workers, and businesses.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="/about/">Read Roy’s profile</a>
            <a class="button secondary" href="/ideas/">Explore his ideas</a>
          </div>
          <p class="lang-note">This is Roy’s personal website. It is not an official campaign site. 中文信息请见 <a href="/zh/">中文版页面</a>。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-card">
          <div class="portrait-placeholder"></div>
          <h2>I work for people, not bureaucrats.</h2>
          <p>For Roy, good government starts with common sense: safe streets, balanced books, less bureaucracy, fewer unnecessary barriers, and real respect for the people who build, work, invest, and raise families in British Columbia.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Common sense priorities</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Roy is currently sharing his personal background and public-policy views while considering service in Vancouver-Langara. His focus is aligned with a common sense conservative direction: restore public safety, balance the budget, reduce red tape, and get B.C. working again.</p>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>Responsible government</h3><p>British Columbia needs common sense change: a government that is prudent, accountable, and focused on results instead of bureaucracy and slogans.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Balanced budgets</h3><p>Public money is not abstract. Deficits today become taxes, inflation, or reduced choices tomorrow. A serious government must live within reality.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Public safety</h3><p>Safe streets, safe transit, safe schools, and safe neighbourhoods must come first. Public safety is the foundation of freedom and community life.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section split">
      <div class="quote">“A province cannot build confidence if families feel unsafe, businesses feel punished, and government spends as if consequences do not exist.”</div>
      <div class="list">
        <div class="list-item"><strong>Business and innovation</strong> Roy understands how builders think. A healthy province needs entrepreneurs, investment, jobs, lower barriers, and the confidence to build here.</div>
        <div class="list-item"><strong>Vancouver-Langara</strong> A community of families, professionals, seniors, students, homeowners, renters, and entrepreneurs deserves a serious voice.</div>
        <div class="list-item"><strong>Public trust</strong> Government must be able to explain what it is doing, what it costs, and why it works.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section split">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Follow Roy</div>
        <h2>Ideas, public notes, and professional updates.</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Roy is building an English-language public profile around responsible government, public safety, balanced budgets, technology, business, and less red tape. More channels will be added as they are ready.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="list">
        <div class="list-item"><strong>LinkedIn</strong> Follow Roy’s professional background and updates. <br /><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/roy-li-2a4248217/">View LinkedIn profile</a></div>
        <div class="list-item"><strong>Writing</strong> Short English notes on British Columbia, business, public safety, and responsible government will appear here.</div>
        <div class="list-item"><strong>Community conversations</strong> For speaking, media, or local conversations in Vancouver-Langara, use the contact page.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="cta">
        <div>
          <h2>Connect with Roy.</h2>
          <p>For community conversations, media inquiries, or to share issues facing Vancouver-Langara and British Columbia.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
